  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we need to find the volume of one box.\n\nWe can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=10,\\,w=8,\\,h=8\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V=10\\cdot 8\\cdot 8=640\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total volume of the seven storage boxes is\n\n$$\n640\\cdot 7=4\\,480\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
